# Mini-Pautas System - Project Configuration

## Environment Variables

```bash
# .env.example - Copy to .env.local for development

# Supabase Configuration
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://afueujnyeglgnaylaxmp.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# Application Configuration
VITE_APP_NAME=Mini-Pautas
VITE_APP_VERSION=1.0.0
VITE_APP_ENV=development

# After applying supabase/migrations/20261105_perf_auth_bootstrap_and_rls.sql:
# VITE_AUTH_BOOTSTRAP=true

# Optional: Analytics
VITE_ANALYTICS_ID=
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# Backend / Edge Functions (nunca no frontend)
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...

# Payment webhooks (Edge Function payment-webhook)
# HMAC-SHA256 of raw body; header x-signature (hex or sha256=<hex>)
# Secrets podem ficar para mais tarde — até lá, em DEV:
# SKIP_WEBHOOK_VERIFICATION=true
# EMIS_GPO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# PROXYPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# APPYPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# MANUAL_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# ENVIRONMENT=development
# (SKIP é rejeitado se ENVIRONMENT=production)
```

## Important Notes

> [!CAUTION]
> **NEVER commit the actual `.env.local` file to version control!**
> 
> The `.env.example` file should only contain placeholder values.
> Actual keys must be obtained from the Supabase dashboard.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Service Role Key Security**
> 
> The `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` should NEVER be used in frontend code.
> It bypasses all Row Level Security policies and should only be used in:
> - Edge Functions (server-side)
> - Backend scripts
> - Database migrations

## Getting Your Supabase Keys

1. Go to your Supabase project dashboard
2. Navigate to Settings → API
3. Copy the following:
   - **Project URL**: Use for `VITE_SUPABASE_URL`
   - **anon public**: Use for `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`
   - **service_role**: Only for backend (never in frontend)

## Setup Instructions

```bash
# 1. Clone the repository
git clone <repository-url>
cd dark-hubble

# 2. Install dependencies
npm install

# 3. Copy environment template
cp .env.example .env.local

# 4. Edit .env.local and add your actual keys
nano .env.local

# 5. Run development server
npm run dev
```
